<nav class="cm-rail" aria-label="Timeline stops"><div class="cm-rail-track" aria-hidden="true"></div><a href="#stop-1" data-stop="1" aria-label="2004–2018 — Boulder, then my own studio"><span class="cm-rail-dot"></span><span class="cm-rail-date">2004–2018</span></a><a href="#stop-2" data-stop="2" aria-label="2018 — Menlo Park or Denver"><span class="cm-rail-dot"></span><span class="cm-rail-date">2018</span></a><a href="#stop-3" data-stop="3" aria-label="2018–2021 — Visible (Verizon)"><span class="cm-rail-dot"></span><span class="cm-rail-date">2018–2021</span></a><a href="#stop-4" data-stop="4" aria-label="2021–2023 — Synack"><span class="cm-rail-dot"></span><span class="cm-rail-date">2021–2023</span></a><a href="#stop-5" data-stop="5" aria-label="2023–now — State of Colorado"><span class="cm-rail-dot"></span><span class="cm-rail-date">2023–now</span></a><a href="#stop-6" data-stop="6" aria-label="2026–now — Rendered Intent"><span class="cm-rail-dot"></span><span class="cm-rail-date">2026–now</span></a></nav>
<div class="cm-stops"><article id="stop-1" data-start-year="2004" class="cm-stop cm-stop-1 " tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="title-1"><div class="cm-stop-meta"><span>2004–2018</span></div><div class="cm-stop-copy"><h3 id="title-1">Boulder, then my own studio</h3><p>I started at Sterling-Rice Group, an ad agency in Boulder, in 2004. In 2006, I left to freelance for startups. One-off projects grew into year-long retainers, then into indiegraphic, the product design studio I founded. I worked with bootstrapped startups and Fortune 50 companies across Denver, Boulder, San Francisco, New York, Seattle, Austin, Toronto, Bangalore, and Singapore. Working across languages, cultures, and time zones called for patience, careful listening, and checking my understanding before moving ahead.</p></div></article><article id="stop-2" data-start-year="2018" class="cm-stop cm-stop-2 " tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="title-2"><div class="cm-stop-meta"><span>2018</span></div><div class="cm-stop-copy"><h3 id="title-2">Menlo Park or Denver</h3><p>Facebook flew me out to Menlo Park to meet some teams. At the same time, Verizon called about a stealth project in Denver. I chose Denver for the 0→1 work, and that project became Visible.</p></div><div class="cm-studio-transition" role="img" aria-label="From indiegraphic, an independent studio, to in-house product work: Verizon’s stealth project in Denver became Visible.">
  <div class="cm-studio-origin" aria-hidden="true">
    <strong>indiegraphic</strong>
    <small>Independent studio</small>
  </div>
  <span class="cm-studio-connector" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <div class="cm-studio-destination" aria-hidden="true">
    <strong><span>Verizon</span> <span class="cm-studio-arrow">→</span> Visible</strong>
    <small>Denver · 0→1</small>
  </div>
</div>
</article><article id="stop-3" data-start-year="2018" class="cm-stop cm-stop-3 " tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="title-3"><div class="cm-stop-meta"><span>2018–2021</span></div><div class="cm-stop-copy"><h3 id="title-3">Visible (Verizon)</h3><p>I led design across growth and member experience, from ecommerce and eSIM activation to <a href="https://tomsguide.com/news/visible-party-pay-drops-your-phone-bill-by-up-to-dollar15-per-month" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-describedby="cm-new-tab-note" title="Opens in a new tab"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">Party </span><span class="cm-intro-link-end"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">Pay</span><svg class="cm-intro-link-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12 12 4M4 4h8v8"/></svg></span></a> and Visible&#x27;s first design system, and some of that work carried over into Verizon. Senior, then Principal. Later I moved into Verizon&#x27;s wider design org and spent a year leading a Verizon design team in India, keeping work moving across opposite time zones.</p><div class="cm-studio-transition cm-role-progression" role="img" aria-label="Promoted from Senior to Principal at Visible."><div class="cm-studio-origin" aria-hidden="true"><strong>Senior</strong></div><span class="cm-studio-connector" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="cm-studio-destination" aria-hidden="true"><strong>Principal</strong></div></div><a class="cm-stop-link" href="#visible-case" aria-describedby="cm-inpage-note" title="Jumps to a section on this page"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">View </span><span class="cm-intro-link-end"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">work</span><svg class="cm-intro-link-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 3v10M4 9l4 4 4-4"/></svg></span></a></div></article><article id="stop-4" data-start-year="2021" class="cm-stop cm-stop-4 " tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="title-4"><div class="cm-stop-meta"><span>2021–2023</span></div><div class="cm-stop-copy"><h3 id="title-4">Synack</h3><p>I designed workflows for Synack’s FedRAMP-authorized penetration-testing platform, connecting enterprises and federal agencies with vetted security researchers to find and validate vulnerabilities. I worked closely with my product manager to build a team where people could challenge ideas, give honest feedback, and bring their own thinking to the work.<span class="cm-redaction-row"><button type="button" class="cm-redaction" aria-describedby="cm-redaction-hint"><span class="cm-redaction-text">The work itself stays off the record.</span></button></span><span id="cm-redaction-hint" hidden>Hover, focus or activate to reveal visually.</span></p><a class="cm-stop-link" href="https://www.synack.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-describedby="cm-new-tab-note" title="Opens in a new tab"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">About </span><span class="cm-intro-link-end"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">Synack</span><svg class="cm-intro-link-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12 12 4M4 4h8v8"/></svg></span></a></div></article><div class="cm-parallel"><article id="stop-5" data-start-year="2023" class="cm-stop cm-stop-5 " tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="title-5"><div class="cm-stop-meta"><span class="cm-current-period">2023–now</span></div><div class="cm-stop-copy"><h3 id="title-5">State of Colorado</h3><p>Design lead on myColorado, the state&#x27;s official app, with more than <a href="https://oit.colorado.gov/press-release/governor-polis-celebrates-over-2-million-registered-users-on-mycolorador-states" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-describedby="cm-new-tab-note" title="Opens in a new tab"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">2 million registered </span><span class="cm-intro-link-end"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">users</span><svg class="cm-intro-link-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12 12 4M4 4h8v8"/></svg></span></a>. I work across product, brand and digital identity, on a design system I built from scratch for iOS and Android, with WCAG 2.2 AA as the design target. I helped our team unblock a long-running mobile driver&#x27;s license initiative and bring it to launch. I was <a href="https://x.com/GovofCO/status/2094562971292762554" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-describedby="cm-new-tab-note" title="Opens in a new tab"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">invited to DIA with the </span><span class="cm-intro-link-end"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">team</span><svg class="cm-intro-link-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12 12 4M4 4h8v8"/></svg></span></a> for the governor&#x27;s announcement.</p><div class="cm-shipped"><h4>Shipped</h4><dl><div class="cm-shipped-entry"><dt><a href="https://www.tsa.gov/news/press/releases/2026/08/31/tsa-accepts-mycolorado-mdls-during-identity-verification" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-describedby="cm-new-tab-note" title="Opens in a new tab"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">Mobile driver&#x27;s </span><span class="cm-intro-link-end"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">license</span><svg class="cm-intro-link-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12 12 4M4 4h8v8"/></svg></span></a></dt><dd>accepted by TSA at more than 250 airports</dd></div><div class="cm-shipped-entry"><dt><a href="https://oit.colorado.gov/press-release/introducing-the-colorado-digital-idtm-verifier-in-mycolorador" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-describedby="cm-new-tab-note" title="Opens in a new tab"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">Digital ID </span><span class="cm-intro-link-end"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">Verifier</span><svg class="cm-intro-link-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12 12 4M4 4h8v8"/></svg></span></a></dt><dd>so businesses can spot counterfeit IDs</dd></div><div class="cm-shipped-entry"><dt><a href="https://mycolorado.gov/mycolorado-mdl/mdl-reader" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-describedby="cm-new-tab-note" title="Opens in a new tab"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">mDL </span><span class="cm-intro-link-end"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">Reader</span><svg class="cm-intro-link-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12 12 4M4 4h8v8"/></svg></span></a></dt><dd>which checks age from Apple, Google and Samsung wallets, <a href="https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/platforms/google-pay/google-wallet-update-september-2024/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-describedby="cm-new-tab-note" title="Opens in a new tab"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">highlighted by Google </span><span class="cm-intro-link-end"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">Wallet</span><svg class="cm-intro-link-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12 12 4M4 4h8v8"/></svg></span></a></dd></div></dl></div></div></article><article id="stop-6" data-start-year="2026" class="cm-stop cm-stop-6 " tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="title-6"><div class="cm-stop-meta"><span class="cm-side-note">Evenings and weekends</span></div><div class="cm-stop-copy"><h3 id="title-6">Rendered Intent</h3><p>My ongoing exploration of how AI changes product work. Rendered Intent keeps the reasoning next to the work, in a project brain that people and AI tools can build from. This site is the working example: I shape it with Claude and ChatGPT, Claude Code and Codex build it from the brain, and it&#x27;ll keep changing as I learn.</p><a class="cm-stop-link" href="https://renderedintent.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-describedby="cm-new-tab-note" title="Opens in a new tab"><span class="cm-intro-link-text"></span><span class="cm-intro-link-end"><span class="cm-intro-link-text">renderedintent.com</span><svg class="cm-intro-link-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12 12 4M4 4h8v8"/></svg></span></a></div></article></div></div></div></section>